## Plan

_Written by `claude-3` (claude, `sonnet`, medium) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/45880144245)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

## Goal

A pull request that changes a card also runs, in `e2e smoke`, the specs whose seeded games deal or name that card, capped at 120 s of `WEIGHTS` per shard. Done is:
- `jackioh changed-cards [--json] [--root <dir>]` names a pull request's changed cards. It names none (exit 0, with a note) off a two-parent merge commit or with an unreadable base.
- `e2e/scripts/shard-specs.mjs --smoke` adds the reached specs up to the budget and logs why. Named specs come first, then fixture-only ones, lightest first, ties by file name. 46 and 47 never join.
- With no binary, no changed card, the merge queue or `main`, the list stays `SMOKE`.

The code below is a prototype I ran on the real specs and fixtures, and it passed eslint. core-077 adds 03 and 29 (named) and 15 more, 480 of 480 s. core-093 adds only 28. core-025 adds 475 s and leaves 15.

## Files to touch

| File | | What |
|---|---|---|
| `crates/tools/src/changed.rs` | change | `Serialize` on `Changed`; `Args`, `run`, `render`, `pull_request_cards`, `NOT_A_MERGE`; header lines; tests |
| `crates/tools/src/main.rs` | change | `Command::ChangedCards` and its `match` arm |
| `crates/tools/README.md` | change | one command-table row |
| `e2e/scripts/shard-specs.mjs` | change | selection, budget constant, `JACKIOH_BIN`, log, header comment |
| `e2e/README.md` | change | a paragraph beside the smoke-list sentence |
| `apps/web/src/net/e2e-smoke-selection.test.ts` | new | vitest: the selection and the CLI wiring |

Do not touch `.github/`, `bot/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `scripts/ci-shards.toml` (the count stays 4), `scripts/ci-scope.sh` (a card change already turns `e2e` on through its `*) on e2e`), `crates/tools/tests/acceptance.rs`, or any spec or fixture. No ruling and no patch fragment: no game rule or catalog entry changes.

## Steps

1. **`crates/tools/src/changed.rs`.** Imports: `use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};`, `use serde::Serialize;`, `use crate::patches::{git, repo_root};`. Add `Serialize` to `Changed`'s derive. After `changed_cards` add:
   ```rust
   const NOT_A_MERGE: &str = "HEAD is not a two-parent merge commit (a pull request's), so no card is named";

   #[derive(clap::Args, Debug)]
   pub struct Args {
       /// The repository root (default: the workspace this binary was built from).
       #[arg(long)]
       root: Option<PathBuf>,
       /// Print the cards, notes and warning as one JSON object.
       #[arg(long)]
       json: bool,
   }

   /// The cards a pull request changes, none unless `HEAD` is its merge commit and its base reads:
   /// `changed_cards` alone falls back to every pending fragment's cards, which in the merge queue's
   /// one-parent commit and on `main` no pull request changed (#5099).
   pub(crate) fn pull_request_cards(root: &Path) -> Changed {
       if merge_base(root).is_none() {
           return Changed { notes: vec![NOT_A_MERGE.to_string()], ..Changed::default() };
       }
       let changed = changed_cards(root);
       if changed.warning.is_some() {
           return Changed { warning: changed.warning, ..Changed::default() };
       }
       changed
   }

   fn render(changed: &Changed, json: bool) -> anyhow::Result<String> {
       if json {
           return Ok(serde_json::to_string_pretty(changed)?);
       }
       let mut lines = vec![if changed.ids.is_empty() {
           "changed cards: none".to_string()
       } else {
           format!("changed cards: {}", changed.ids.join(", "))
       }];
       lines.extend(changed.notes.iter().cloned());
       lines.extend(changed.warning.iter().map(|warning| format!("warning: {warning}")));
       Ok(lines.join("\n"))
   }

   /// `jackioh changed-cards`: prints and exits 0 whatever it finds; shard-specs.mjs reads its `--json`.
   pub fn run(args: Args) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
       let root = args.root.unwrap_or_else(repo_root);
       println!("{}", render(&pull_request_cards(&root), args.json)?);
       Ok(())
   }
   ```
   `--json` prints `{"ids": [...], "notes": [...], "warning": null | "..."}`, the contract the script reads. Add two `//!` header lines: the module also serves `jackioh changed-cards` (#5099).
2. **`crates/tools/src/main.rs`.** Beside `Classify` add `/// The cards a pull request changes, as fuzz's gate reads them; none off a merge commit (#5099).` and `ChangedCards(changed::Args),`. In the `match`, add `Command::ChangedCards(args) => changed::run(args),`.
3. **`crates/tools/README.md`.** After the `classify` row add a row. The first cell is exactly `` `changed-cards [--root <dir>] [--json]` `` and the module is `` `changed.rs` ``. The Does cell says:
   - the cards a pull request changes as `fuzz`'s gate reads them (`changed_cards`, #3113);
   - it prints them, the notes and any warning (`--json`: `{"ids", "notes", "warning"}`);
   - it names none, exit 0 with a note, when `HEAD` is not a two-parent merge commit (the merge queue's squash commit, `main`, a local branch) or the base cannot be read, since the fragments-only fallback would name every pending patch's cards there;
   - `shard-specs.mjs --smoke` reads it (#5099).

   Never write "e2e spec" in the cell: `acceptance.rs` reads "e2e spec <n> checks…" as a citation.
4. **`e2e/scripts/shard-specs.mjs`, constants.** Imports: `execFileSync` from `node:child_process`; `existsSync, readdirSync, readFileSync` from `node:fs`. After `COMPONENT_DIR`: `const DECK_DIR = "fixtures/decks";`, `const JACKIOH_BIN = "target/release/jackioh";`, `const CHANGED_CARDS_TIMEOUT_MS = 60_000;` (the base's fetch included). After `SMOKE`: `export const SMOKE_EXTRA_BUDGET_S = 120;` and `const NEVER_ADDED = ["46", "47"];` (#4092, number prefixes). The budget's doc says: seconds of `WEIGHTS` a pull request's extra specs may add per shard (#5099); today's heaviest smoke shard is 82 s, and shards of about 285 s ran 8m 7s and 8m 57s (#3764).
5. **Same file, `specWeight`.** Add `export function specWeight(spec) { return WEIGHTS[spec.slice(0, 2)] ?? DEFAULT_WEIGHT; }` above `shardSpecs`. Make `shardSpecs`'s default `weight` parameter `specWeight`. Change nothing else there.
6. **Same file, selection** (above the `if (process.argv[1] === …)` block):
   ```js
   function quotes(text, word) {
     return ['"', "'", "`"].some((quote) => text.includes(`${quote}${word}${quote}`));
   }

   /** Spec -> { how, cards }: "names" when its source quotes a changed card's id or catalog name, else "deals" when it quotes the id of a fixture deck holding one. */
   export function reachedSpecs(ids, specs, { sources, decks, names }) {
     const reached = new Map();
     for (const spec of specs) {
       if (NEVER_ADDED.includes(spec.slice(0, 2))) continue;
       const text = sources[spec];
       const named = ids.filter((id) => quotes(text, id) || (names[id] !== undefined && quotes(text, names[id])));
       const dealt = ids.filter((id) => Object.entries(decks).some(([deck, cards]) => cards.includes(id) && quotes(text, deck)));
       if (named.length > 0) reached.set(spec, { how: "names", cards: named });
       else if (dealt.length > 0) reached.set(spec, { how: "deals", cards: dealt });
     }
     return reached;
   }

   /** SMOKE, then the reached specs, "names" before "deals", each lightest first (ties by file name), while their weights total at most SMOKE_EXTRA_BUDGET_S * count. The first spec past the budget and all after it are `left` to the daily run. */
   export function smokeSelection(every, ids, count, world) {
     const smoke = smokeSpecs(every);
     const reached = reachedSpecs(ids, every.filter((spec) => !smoke.includes(spec)), world);
     const rank = (spec) => (reached.get(spec).how === "names" ? 0 : 1);
     const order = [...reached.keys()].sort((a, b) => rank(a) - rank(b) || specWeight(a) - specWeight(b) || (a < b ? -1 : 1));
     const budget = SMOKE_EXTRA_BUDGET_S * count;
     const added = [];
     const left = [];
     let load = 0;
     for (const spec of order) {
       if (left.length === 0 && load + specWeight(spec) <= budget) {
         added.push(spec);
         load += specWeight(spec);
       } else {
         left.push(spec);
       }
     }
     return { specs: [...smoke, ...added], added, left, load, budget, reached };
   }

   /** `root` is e2e/. */
   export function readWorld(root, ids) {
     const sources = {};
     for (const name of readdirSync(join(root, SPEC_DIR))) {
       if (name.endsWith(".cy.ts")) sources[name] = readFileSync(join(root, SPEC_DIR, name), "utf8");
     }
     const decks = {};
     for (const name of readdirSync(join(root, DECK_DIR))) {
       if (!name.endsWith(".json")) continue;
       const deck = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(root, DECK_DIR, name), "utf8"));
       decks[deck.id ?? name.slice(0, -".json".length)] = deck.cards;
     }
     const catalog = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(root, "..", "crates/cards/catalog.json"), "utf8"));
     const names = Object.fromEntries(ids.filter((id) => catalog[id]?.name !== undefined).map((id) => [id, catalog[id].name]));
     return { sources, decks, names };
   }
   ```
7. **Same file, the binary and the log** (before the `if` block):
   ```js
   function log(line) {
     process.stderr.write(`smoke: ${line}\n`);
   }

   /** `jackioh changed-cards --json` from JACKIOH_BIN (default ../target/release/jackioh); undefined with no binary (a local run) or when it fails: the list then stays SMOKE. */
   function changedCards(root) {
     const bin = process.env.JACKIOH_BIN ?? join(root, "..", JACKIOH_BIN);
     if (!existsSync(bin)) return undefined;
     try {
       const out = execFileSync(bin, ["changed-cards", "--json", "--root", join(root, "..")], {
         encoding: "utf8",
         stdio: ["ignore", "pipe", "inherit"],
         timeout: CHANGED_CARDS_TIMEOUT_MS,
       });
       const changed = JSON.parse(out);
       if (!Array.isArray(changed.ids) || !Array.isArray(changed.notes)) throw new Error("no ids and notes in its output");
       return changed;
     } catch (error) {
       log(`${bin} changed-cards failed (${error.message}); the list stays SMOKE`);
       return undefined;
     }
   }

   function logSelection(changed, { added, left, load, budget, reached }) {
     log(`${changed.ids.length} changed cards: ${changed.ids.join(", ")}`);
     for (const spec of added) {
       const { how, cards } = reached.get(spec);
       log(`+ ${spec} (${specWeight(spec)} s) ${how} ${cards.join(", ")}`);
     }
     log(`${added.length} extra specs, ${load} of ${budget} s (${SMOKE_EXTRA_BUDGET_S} s a shard)`);
     if (left.length > 0) log(`left to the daily run: ${left.join(", ")}`);
   }
   ```
8. **Same file, the CLI block.** In `if (smoke) { … }`, after the `try/catch` that sets `specs = smokeSpecs(every)`:
   ```js
   const changed = changedCards(root);
   if (changed !== undefined && changed.ids.length > 0) {
     const selection = smokeSelection(every, changed.ids, count, readWorld(root, changed.ids));
     specs = selection.specs;
     logSelection(changed, selection);
   } else if (changed !== undefined) {
     const why = changed.warning ? [...changed.notes, changed.warning] : changed.notes;
     log(`no changed cards${why.map((note) => `; ${note}`).join("")}`);
   }
   ```
   Stdout stays the shard's comma-separated list (the action captures it with `$(…)`); every log line goes to stderr. Update the header comment: a pull request's `--smoke` is SMOKE plus the specs its changed cards reach (#5099).
9. **`e2e/README.md`.** After "Specs 46 and 47 run in the daily super run only (#4092)…" add the paragraph below:
   - A pull request that changes a card also plays the specs whose games deal or name it (#5099).
   - `--smoke` asks the release `jackioh changed-cards --json` (`JACKIOH_BIN` overrides the path). With no binary, as locally, or in the merge queue and on `main`, it stays `SMOKE`.
   - It adds each spec that quotes a changed card's id or catalog name, then each that quotes the id of a `fixtures/decks/*.json` deck holding one. They go lightest first by `WEIGHTS`, while their weights total at most `SMOKE_EXTRA_BUDGET_S` (120 s) a shard.
   - The rest is printed as left to the daily run. 46 and 47 never join.
10. Write the tests below and run the commands.

## Tests

**`crates/tools/src/changed.rs`, `mod tests`** (reuse `TempRepo`, `base_repo`, `fragment`, `pending`, `entry`, `catalog`, `CATALOG`, `SCRIPT`, `ZEROS`):
- Move the planting block of `a_base_the_clone_lacks_and_cannot_fetch_is_reported_not_fatal` (`let tree = …` through the `checkout --detach`) into `fn plant_merge_over_missing_base(repo: &TempRepo)` and call it there. Behaviour is unchanged.
- `fn core_077(health: i32) -> String` builds `"core-077": { "id": "core-077", "name": "Professor Curvature", "cost": 3, "health": N }`.
- `a_pull_requests_merge_names_the_card_whose_health_its_second_parent_changed`:
  - The base commit is `catalog(&[entry("core-001", 1, "a"), core_077(3)])`. Branch `topic` writes `core_077(5)`. On `main` commit `main.txt`, then `git merge -q --no-ff -m merge topic` (copy the existing merge test).
  - `pull_request_cards(..).ids == ["core-077"]`, no warning.
  - `render(.., true)` parses (`serde_json::Value`) with `["ids"] == json!(["core-077"])` and `["warning"].is_null()`.
- `a_commit_that_is_no_merge_names_no_card_even_with_pending_patches`: `base_repo`, commit `pending("a.json")` = `fragment(r#""core-002""#, "")`. Assert:
  - `changed_cards(..).ids == ["core-002"]`;
  - `pull_request_cards(..) == Changed { ids: vec![], notes: vec![NOT_A_MERGE.to_string()], warning: None }`;
  - `run(Args { root: Some(repo.path().to_path_buf()), json: true }).is_ok()`.
- `an_unreadable_base_names_no_card_even_with_pending_patches`: commit the same fragment, then `plant_merge_over_missing_base`. `pull_request_cards` has empty `ids` and `notes`, and a `warning` containing `ZEROS`.
- `plain_output_lists_the_ids_the_notes_and_the_warning`: `render` of `Changed { ids: ["core-077"], notes: ["n"], warning: Some("w") }` is `"changed cards: core-077\nn\nwarning: w"`. `Changed::default()` gives `"changed cards: none"`.

**`apps/web/src/net/e2e-smoke-selection.test.ts`** (new; header comment like `ci-scope.test.ts`'s; test names start `#5099`).
- Setup:
  - `E2E = join(HERE, "../../../../e2e")` and `SCRIPT = join(E2E, "scripts/shard-specs.mjs")`.
  - Name no `crates/…` path in a literal (`ci-scope.test.ts` scans web sources for paths).
  - Load the module with `(await import(pathToFileURL(SCRIPT).href)) as Script`, where `Script` is an interface in the test (`SMOKE`, `SMOKE_EXTRA_BUDGET_S`, `specWeight`, `shardSpecs`, `smokeSpecs`, `smokeSelection`, `readWorld`). I ran this import under vitest and it works, with no `@ts-expect-error`.
  - `every` is the `.cy.ts` names in `join(E2E, "cypress/e2e")`. `select(ids, count = 4)` is `smokeSelection(every, ids, count, readWorld(E2E, ids))`.
- core-077: `specs` holds `29-animated-trap.cy.ts`, `03-trap-opponent-turn.cy.ts` and every `smokeSpecs(every)` file.
- core-093: `specs` holds `28-patch-011-ui.cy.ts`.
- No changed card: `select([]).specs` equals `smokeSpecs(every)`; `added` is empty.
- core-025:
  - `load <= SMOKE_EXTRA_BUDGET_S * 4`, and it equals the `specWeight` sum of `added`.
  - Over `added`, `reached.get(spec).how` has no "deals" before a "names".
  - `left` is non-empty and shares no spec with `added`.
